Header
  + name := Hello_world
/*
  The basic and traditional "Hello World" program in Lisaac Ω.
  It prints one line in the terminal.

  Shows: the smallest complete program, a prototype with a single
  slot `main', where the execution starts.

  To compile, as usual in a terminal:
  $ cd lisaac/example
  $ lisaac hello_world -q -boost
  $ ./hello_world

  Or in one single step with bash:
  $ run=hello_world ; lisaac ${run} -q -boost && ./${run}
  */
Public
  
  - main <-
  (
    print("Hello world!\n")
  )
  
  